{"name":"Fenland","hex":"#ac9d83","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fenland","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A local government district of Cambridgeshire, England."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fenland"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Fens","blocks":[{"text":"The Fens or Fenlands in eastern England are a naturally marshy region supporting a rich ecology and numerous species. Most of the fens were drained centuries ago, resulting in a flat, dry, low-lying agricultural region supported by a system of drainage channels, man-made rivers, and automated pumping stations. There have been unintended consequences to this reclamation, as the land level has continued to sink and the dykes have been built higher to protect it from flooding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Wicken-Fen-Hide.jpg/330px-Wicken-Fen-Hide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fens"},{"title":"Fenland District","blocks":[{"text":"Fenland is a local government district in Cambridgeshire, England. It was historically part of the Isle of Ely. The district covers around 500 square kilometres (190 sq mi) of mostly agricultural land in the extremely flat Fens. The council is based in Fenland Hall, in March. Other towns include Chatteris, Whittlesey and Wisbech, the largest of the four."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/On_the_town_bridge_in_March_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3108774.jpg/330px-On_the_town_bridge_in_March_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3108774.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fenland_District"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/London%2C_Great_Britain_Population_Density_and_Low_Elevation_Coastal_Zones_%285457306673%29.jpg/500px-London%2C_Great_Britain_Population_Density_and_Low_Elevation_Coastal_Zones_%285457306673%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/London%2C_Great_Britain_Population_Density_and_Low_Elevation_Coastal_Zones_%285457306673%29.jpg/1280px-London%2C_Great_Britain_Population_Density_and_Low_Elevation_Coastal_Zones_%285457306673%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/London%2C_Great_Britain_Population_Density_and_Low_Elevation_Coastal_Zones_%285457306673%29.jpg/500px-London%2C_Great_Britain_Population_Density_and_Low_Elevation_Coastal_Zones_%285457306673%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"England population density and low elevation coastal zones. The Fens are particularly vulnerable to sea level rise.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALondon%2C_Great_Britain_Population_Density_and_Low_Elevation_Coastal_Zones_(5457306673).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Wicken_Fen_Windpump.jpg/500px-Wicken_Fen_Windpump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Wicken_Fen_Windpump.jpg/1280px-Wicken_Fen_Windpump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Wicken_Fen_Windpump.jpg/500px-Wicken_Fen_Windpump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A windpump at Wicken Fen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWicken_Fen_Windpump.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Bylaws_for_the_drainage_of_Deeping_Fen_%28geograph_3691189%29.jpg/500px-Bylaws_for_the_drainage_of_Deeping_Fen_%28geograph_3691189%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb